{"id":3180,"path":"/grammar-points/a2/first-conditional-future-time-clauses/","parentId":542,"order":180,"section":"grammar-points","level":"a2","depth":3,"title":"First conditional and future time clauses","seo":{"title":"First conditional and future time clauses - Test-English","description":"Learn the first conditional and future time clauses in this A2 Pre-intermediate grammar lesson. Clear rules, charts and exercises!","image":"/media/uploads/A2-First-conditional_Future-time-clauses.png"},"modified":"2026-02-21T11:03:51","kind":"lesson","parts":["<h3>Exercise 1</h3> <h5>Choose the correct forms to complete the first conditional sentences below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"387\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 2</h3> <h5>Choose the correct forms to complete the first conditional sentences and future time clauses below.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"388\"></div>","<h3>Exercise 3</h3> <h5>Complete the following first conditional sentences with the verbs in brackets in the correct form. Use<em> will/won’t</em> in the main clause.</h5> <div data-quiz=\"389\"></div>"],"explanation":"<h2>First conditional: Grammar Chart</h2> <p><img class=\"alignleft size-full wp-image-13280\" src=\"/media/uploads/first-conditional-B1_new.png\" alt=\"First conditional B1\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4><strong>If</strong> clause and main clause</h4> <p>All conditional sentences have two parts: the <strong>if<em>&nbsp;</em>clause </strong>and the <strong>main clause</strong>. It doesn’t matter which clause comes first, but when the&nbsp;<strong>if clause</strong>&nbsp;comes first, we should put a <strong>comma</strong> after it.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><strong><em>If</em></strong></span><em> it rains<span><strong>,</strong></span> we’ll stay home</em></li> <li><em>We’ll stay home <span><strong>if</strong></span> it rains.</em></li> </ul> <h4><strong>If</strong> + present, future</h4> <p>In the first conditional, the verb in the&nbsp;<strong>if<em>&nbsp;</em>clause</strong>&nbsp;is <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/present-simple/\">present</a>, and the verb in the <strong>main clause</strong> is <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/will-and-shall/\">future</a>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><strong><em>If</em></strong></span><em> you <span><strong>don’t go </strong></span>to sleep, you’<span><strong>ll be </strong></span>very tired tomorrow.</em></li> </ul> <p>The<b><i>&nbsp;</i><strong>if&nbsp;clause&nbsp;</strong></b>may have a present or a future meaning, but the <strong>verb</strong> is <strong>always</strong> <strong>in the present</strong> (NOT future)</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><span><strong><em>If</em></strong></span><em> you <span><strong>will be </strong></span>a good boy tomorrow, mummy will buy you a present. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><span><strong><em>If</em></strong></span><em> you <span><strong>are </strong></span>a good boy tomorrow, mummy will buy you a present. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4>Main clause: <strong>will</strong>, modal verb, imperative</h4> <p>In the <strong>main clause</strong>, we can also use <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/may-and-might-whats-the-difference/\"><strong>may, might</strong></a>, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/can-cant/\"><strong>can</strong></a>, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/have-to-dont-have-to-must-mustnt/\"><strong>must</strong></a>, <a href=\"/grammar-points/a2/should-shouldnt/\"><strong>should</strong></a> instead of <strong>will</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>If he doesn’t train harder, he <span><strong>may/might</strong></span> lose the championship. </em></li> <li><em>If your room is tidy, you <span><strong>can</strong></span> leave.</em></li> <li><em>If you want to lose weight, you <span><strong>must/should</strong></span> eat less sugary things.</em></li> </ul> <p>We can also use an <a href=\"/grammar-points/a1/imperative-sit-dont-talk/\">imperative</a> instead of <strong>will</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>If</em><em> you arrive after midnight, <span><strong>ring</strong></span> me on my mobile.</em></li> </ul> <h2>Future time clauses – Grammar Chart</h2> <p><img class=\"alignleft size-full wp-image-13283\" src=\"/media/uploads/future-time-clauses-B1.png\" alt=\"Future time clauses B1\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"></p> <h6></h6> <h4><strong>When, as soon as, before, after, until</strong></h4> <p>When we use a verb after <strong>when, as soon as, before, after </strong>or<strong> until</strong> to talk about the future, we have to use this verb in the present tense (NOT future). We use the future in the other part of the sentence.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I’ll retire when I <span><strong>will be</strong></span></em><em> 70. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>I’ll retire when I</em><em><strong><span>‘m</span></strong></em><em> 70. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>I won’t call you until I <span><strong>will </strong></span></em><span><strong><em>arrive</em></strong></span><em>. <img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21426\" src=\"/media/uploads/wrong.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> <li><em>I won’t&nbsp;call you until I&nbsp;</em><span><strong><em>arrive</em></strong></span><em>.</em> <em><img class=\"alignnone size-full wp-image-21425\" src=\"/media/uploads/correct.png\" alt=\"\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" loading=\"lazy\"></em></li> </ul> <h4>Similar to the first conditional</h4> <p>Future time clauses are similar to the first conditional. There’s a <strong>main clause</strong> and a <strong>when/after/etc. clause</strong>. We use the verbs in these clauses like in the first conditional.</p> <p>We use a comma when the&nbsp;<strong>when/after/etc. clause</strong>&nbsp;is at the beginning of the sentence. But we don’t use a comma if the&nbsp;<strong>when/after/etc. clause</strong>&nbsp;is at the end of the sentence.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>I’</em><strong><em><span>ll</span></em></strong><span> <strong><em>retire</em></strong></span><em> when I’</em><strong><em><span>m</span></em></strong><em>&nbsp;70.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>When I’</em><strong><em><span>m</span></em></strong><em> 70<span><strong>,</strong></span> I’</em><strong><span><em>ll</em> <em>retire</em></span></strong><em>.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>We use the present in the&nbsp;<strong>when/after/etc. clause</strong>, and we use the future in the&nbsp;<strong>main clause</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>Before you </em><span><strong><em>go</em></strong></span><em> to sleep, Daddy </em><span><strong><em>will tell</em></strong></span><em> you a story.&nbsp;</em></li> </ul> <p>In the <strong>main clause</strong>, we can also use <strong>may, might, can, must, should</strong> or an <strong>imperative</strong> instead of <strong>will</strong>.</p> <ul class=\"grammar-ex\"> <li><em>As soon as you finish</em><em>, you </em><span><strong><em>can</em></strong></span><em> leave.&nbsp;</em></li> <li><em>After you arrive</em><em>, </em><span><strong><em>call</em></strong></span><em> me.</em></li> </ul>","quizzes":[{"id":387,"questions":[{"id":3315,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If you <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> now, you <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> the train.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["won't leave","don't leave"]},{"kind":"select","options":["'ll miss","miss"]}]},{"id":3316,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>Peter <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> his exams if he <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> hard.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["will pass","passes"]},{"kind":"select","options":["will work","works"]}]},{"id":3317,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If it <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> tomorrow, we <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> to the cinema.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["will rain","rains"]},{"kind":"select","options":["go","'ll go"]}]},{"id":3318,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>The teacher <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> angry if you <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> late again tomorrow.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["is","will be"]},{"kind":"select","options":["'ll","arrive"]}]},{"id":3319,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> her the news if I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> her next week.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["'ll tell","tell"]},{"kind":"select","options":["'ll see","see"]}]},{"id":3320,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> some takeaway this evening if I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> work late.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["have","'ll have"]},{"kind":"select","options":["finish","'ll finish"]}]},{"id":3321,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If you <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> more, you <span data-gap=\"1\"></span>.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["don't practice","won't practice"]},{"kind":"select","options":["don't improve","won't improve"]}]},{"id":3322,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If we <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the bus, we <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> late.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["don't catch","won't catch"]},{"kind":"select","options":["'ll be","are"]}]},{"id":3323,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>You <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> an accident if you <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> so fast.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["have","might have"]},{"kind":"select","options":["will drive","drive"]}]},{"id":3324,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If you <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to arrive earlier, <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> the train.</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"select","options":["want","'ll want"]},{"kind":"select","options":["take","will take"]}]}]},{"id":388,"questions":[{"id":3329,"num":"1","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>How will you celebrate if you _____ the exams?</div>","choices":[{"id":5500,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>might pass</span>"},{"id":5501,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>will pass</span>"},{"id":5502,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>pass</span>"}]},{"id":3326,"num":"2","type":"checkbox","prompt":"<div>When you see Tom, you ____ surprised to see how much he has changed. <span class=\"highlighter\">Choose TWO correct options</span></div>","maxSelections":2,"choices":[{"id":5491,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>are</span>"},{"id":5492,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>will be</span>"},{"id":5493,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>might be</span>"}]},{"id":3325,"num":"3","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>We won't find peace until we ____ who did this.</div>","choices":[{"id":5488,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>find</span>"},{"id":5489,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>will find</span>"},{"id":5490,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>should find</span>"}]},{"id":3327,"num":"4","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>You will know what true love is as soon as you _____ it.</div>","choices":[{"id":5494,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>find</span>"},{"id":5495,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>will find</span>"},{"id":5496,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>may find</span>"}]},{"id":3330,"num":"5","type":"checkbox","prompt":"<div>If you don't believe me, _____ John. <span class=\"highlighter\">Choose TWO correct options</span></div>","maxSelections":2,"choices":[{"id":5503,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>ask</span>"},{"id":5504,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>you ask</span>"},{"id":5505,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>you should ask</span>"}]},{"id":3331,"num":"6","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>If I _____ a job soon, I won't have enough money for the rent.</div>","choices":[{"id":5506,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>won't find</span>"},{"id":5507,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>don't find</span>"},{"id":5508,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>should find</span>"}]},{"id":3328,"num":"7","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>I _____ it until I see it.</div>","choices":[{"id":5497,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>won't believe</span>"},{"id":5498,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>don't believe</span>"},{"id":5499,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>am not believing</span>"}]},{"id":3332,"num":"8","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>If you open those files attached to your email, your computer ____ infected.</div>","choices":[{"id":5509,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>get</span>"},{"id":5510,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>gets</span>"},{"id":5511,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>might get</span>"}]},{"id":3333,"num":"9","type":"radio","prompt":"<div>When I _____ older, I'll buy a Ferrari.</div>","choices":[{"id":5512,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>am</span>"},{"id":5513,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>might be</span>"},{"id":5514,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>will be</span>"}]},{"id":3334,"num":"10","type":"checkbox","prompt":"<div>If he studies more, he _____ the exam.&nbsp;<span class=\"highlighter\">Choose TWO correct options</span></div>","maxSelections":2,"choices":[{"id":5515,"letter":"A.","html":"<span>pass</span>"},{"id":5516,"letter":"B.","html":"<span>'ll pass</span>"},{"id":5517,"letter":"C.","html":"<span>might pass</span>"}]}]},{"id":389,"questions":[{"id":3335,"num":"1","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If I <span><strong>get up</strong></span> late, I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the bus. (get up/miss)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3336,"num":"2","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the bus, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> late for class. (miss/be)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3337,"num":"3","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> late for class, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> the exam. (be/fail)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3338,"num":"4","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> the exam, my parents <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> angry. (fail/be)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3339,"num":"5","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If my parents <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> angry, they <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> me a guitar. (be/not buy)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3340,"num":"6","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If my parents <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> me a guitar, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> able to take guitar lessons. (not buy/not be)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3341,"num":"7","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> guitar lessons, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> a musician. (not take/not become).</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3342,"num":"8","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> a musician, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> to take a different job. (not become/have)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3343,"num":"9","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> to take a different job, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> very miserable. (have/be)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]},{"id":3344,"num":"10","type":"gaps","prompt":"<p>If I <span data-gap=\"0\"></span> very miserable, I <span data-gap=\"1\"></span> my life. (be/hate)</p>","gaps":[{"kind":"text"},{"kind":"text"}]}]}]}